<!--Post: 482--><!--Time: 1089820395-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST482"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, July 14, 2004 - 8:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->December 11th, &#40;two days after the Nancy Fox murder&#41;, 26 year old Denise Rathburn&#39;s body was found in a frozen creek 12 miles north of Wichita. She had been missing from her home at 5332 E. Pine for 15 days. Dr. Willian Eckert said she died of drowning and exposure. No clues.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 482-->
<!--Post: 597--><!--Time: 1090896833-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST597"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, July 26, 2004 - 7:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My hunch says it&#39;s not a BTK crime.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 597-->
<!--Post: 703--><!--Time: 1091997651-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST703"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, August 08, 2004 - 1:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Unlike him.  According to Tom&#39;s site: <BR> <BR>&#34;Nov. 26, 1977: Denise Rathbun, 26, a mother of two, was last seen pushing a baby carriage full of wet laundry to a coin-operated laundry at Central and Edgemoor. Her body was found two weeks later in a frozen creek in Harvey County. An autopsy showed she had died of drowning and exposure.&#34; <BR> <BR>She wasn&#39;t at home, and there aren&#39;t many clues to suggest she was a BTK victim. <BR> <BR>We would need more information about what the autopsy revealed and her last known path.  My thought is if there was no suggestion of struggle and she was walking near the creek she could&#39;ve slipped in.   <BR> <BR>Then again if her baby carraige was left safe and she was no where near the river then maybe she is a strange BTK victim. <BR> <BR>If the carraige was never found.  Then that could also suggest a BTK victim. <BR> <BR>Overall though this murder went far out of his normal methods.  But let us not forget the Zodiac Killer and the taxi driver.  That was out of the norm and thus we must assume the BTK could be capable of the same deed.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 703-->
<!--Post: 6209--><!--Time: 1107580338-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Newyorker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Newyorker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 9:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe she was a BTK victim.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6209-->
<!--Post: 8032--><!--Time: 1108823972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 19, 2005 - 6:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How close was this body to Marine Hedge and how close to the cereal box. It was found north of Wichita. She disappeared near a laundramat where a few other missing people were last seen. Wichita girl would know where this is, it was out in the booneys.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
