<!--Post: 8465--><!--Time: 1109152834-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8465"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 23, 2005 - 2:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After a little research I found out this was in Harvey Co.It was a few miles north of Delores Davis,and east between Hydraulic and Hillside.I think she was found in a stream under or near a bridge on 133rd This is within a few miles of Delorees but conveniently in another county, different LE little or no communication likely, good way to cover your tracks. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
