<!--Post: 10473--><!--Time: 1109968640-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10473"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 12:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am seeing a pattern to some of these murders that may or may not be rader, the strange thing is that these other questionable unsolved murders have their own pattern and what we now know about Davis this is possibily his work also &#40;Denise&#41; i mean<!--/Text--></td></tr>
