<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10858"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 9:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are 6 murders this year 1977, rader was working for ADT and going to WSU at night, Nancy Fox, 12/8, Denise Rathburn 12/11, Gail Sorenson 2/11, Sandra Talbolt 6/12, Shirley Vian 3/17, Nina Berardi 6/23, motive and opportunity?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10858-->
<!--Post: 10937--><!--Time: 1110312173-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10937"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Km<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Km<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Her baby carriage with the clothes in it was found near the body.  This one always gave me the creeps because it was so close to where the Oteros lived.  Central and Edgemoor &#40;where the laundrymat was at&#41;.  Central and Edgemoor is also where the Dillon&#39;s store is located; that is where the Otero car was found.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10937-->
<!--Post: 12284--><!--Time: 1111863010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12284"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tulip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tulip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 10:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I just read in Beattie&#39;s book, page 71, that Denise kids names were Bryan and Kerri.  Their ages were 3 and 1 respectively &#40;in Dec. 1977&#41;.  Brian &#40;DTDC&#39;s son&#41; would have been 2 and Paula would have been about 3 months pregnant with Kerri.  Also, Denise&#39;s initials are DR and her husband was also in the Air Force.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
